  "hints": [
    "Rotating 90 degrees clockwise moves old cell (r, c) to new position (c, n - 1 - r).",
    "Equivalently, transpose the matrix and then reverse every row: [list(reversed(col)) for col in zip(*matrix)].",
    "Pseudocode:\n  n = len(matrix)\n  return [[matrix[n - 1 - r][c] for r in range(n)] for c in range(n)]"
